<?svml using="@hypit/markup@1"?>

<svml>
  <import from="@hypit/script@1"/>

  <!-- The Script is the only source of spoken words. -->
  <script id="story">
    <opening>
      <HOST> Hypit is not just for talking-head videos. During production, it can call Manim animations directly.
    </opening>

    <mathematics>
      <HOST> @{first!}First, mathematics. The axes unfold, the function curve appears, and the tangent moves along the curve. The change is clear at a glance.
    </mathematics>

    <machine-learning>
      <HOST> @{next!}Next, machine learning. A signal travels from the input layer to the output layer, the weights update, and the loss keeps falling.
    </machine-learning>

    <physics>
      <HOST> @{finally!}Finally, physics. A pendulum, a force vector, and the rules of motion can all be demonstrated clearly.
    </physics>

    <closing>
      <HOST> @{these!}These three animations can share the same production timeline as the narration. At the right moment, the one you need can move into focus.
    </closing>
  </script>
</svml>
